# ISG Uses Katapult Pro for Pole Attachment Engineering

**Customer**: ISG (Interstate Companies)  
**Industry**: Engineering/Architecture  
**Use Case**: Pole Attachment Make-Ready Engineering

## Overview

ISG, a multi-discipline architecture, engineering, and planning firm based in Mankato, MN, has integrated Katapult Pro into their telecommunications division's workflow for pole attachment surveys and make-ready engineering.

## Challenge

As ISG's fiber design practice grew rapidly in response to BEAD funding opportunities, the team needed efficient tools to handle increasing volumes of pole attachment work. Traditional methods were creating bottlenecks in the design-to-permit workflow.

## Solution

ISG integrated Katapult Pro to:
- Capture pole data in the field using mobile applications
- Generate make-ready engineering calculations automatically
- Produce permit-ready pole attachment documentation
- Integrate with their ArcGIS-based design workflow

## Results

- Reduced pole survey time by approximately 40%
- Improved accuracy of make-ready engineering calculations
- Streamlined permit documentation for joint use applications

## Workflow

ISG's current workflow integrates Katapult Pro with ArcGIS for network planning and AutoCAD for construction drawing production. The team uses a combination of in-house staff and project-specific resources to manage peak workloads.

## Quote

*"Katapult Pro has significantly improved our efficiency for pole attachment work. The integration with our GIS workflow has been particularly valuable for managing the data from field surveys through to permit documentation."* - ISG Telecommunications Team
</tool_call>

